	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "Amphenol LTW M12A-08PMMP-SF8001, M12 A-coded 8-pole MALE receptacle, STRAIGHT (180deg) PCB THT, PCB parallel to the panel, mounted from inside (front fastened: body flange hex 18 behind the panel, PG9 nut from outside, nut packed loose), panel 4.5 mm max, IP68 unmated / IP69K mated, 2 A 30 V per contact. Drawing M12A-XXPMMP-SF8001 rev K (27OCT2025) sheet 2 col. 8P: 8x D1.00 for D0.8 pins on D5.50 + centre, 49 deg spacing with a 66 deg gap at the key; cross-checked on the Amphenol STEP (pin tails on hole centres, 0.000 mm). The board rests on the pin shoulders; body flange 3.0-5.0 above the PCB, panel seat (flange front / O-ring face) 5.0, O-ring top 6.8, mating face 26.0; pins 2.5 below the PCB top. Panel cutout on Dwgs.User: D15.4 +/-0.1 with two flats 13.6 +0.1 across, flats at 45 deg to the key. Contact numbering: the sheet 2 layout has no numbers; taken from the sheet 1 front view (IEC 61076-2-101 A-coded male: key up, 1 upper right, 2 upper left, 3 left, 4 lower left, 5 bottom, 6 lower right, 7 right, 8 centre). Tails are straight in line with the contacts (STEP), so the component-side view equals the front view; the key rib at +Y in the STEP sits between contacts 1 and 2. Same pinout as M12A-08PMMR-SF7003: vehicle Hall cables plug in unchanged. Footprint origin = contact 8 = connector (M12 cylinder) axis. https://amphenolltw.com/product-info/M-Series/M-Series.M12(A)/M12A-08PMMP-SF8001.html")
	(tags "M12 A-coding receptacle male 8 pin straight vertical 180deg PCB panel sensor Amphenol LTW IP68")
